SQL CREATE DATABASE Statement

The SQL CREATE DATABASE statement is used to create a new SQL database.

Tip: You need administrative privileges to create a new database.

Syntax
CREATE DATABASE database_name;

MySQL Syntax
CREATE DATABASE database_name;

SQL Server Syntax
CREATE DATABASE database_name;

CREATE DATABASE Example
The following SQL statement creates a database called "testDB":

Example:
CREATE DATABASE testDB;

After the database is created, you can verify it exists by listing databases.

Show Databases
MySQL:
SHOW DATABASES;

SQL Server:
SELECT name FROM sys.databases;

Detailed Notes
- `CREATE DATABASE` creates a new logical database container.
- The database is empty when created, with no tables or data.
- The command usually requires administrative privileges or a user account with database creation rights.
- In some systems, the database name must follow identifier rules (no spaces, no special characters, avoid reserved words).
- In MySQL, you can add optional character set and collation settings:
  CREATE DATABASE testDB CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
- In SQL Server, you can specify file locations and size options:
  CREATE DATABASE testDB
  ON PRIMARY (
      NAME = testDB_data,
      FILENAME = 'C:\Program Files\Microsoft SQL Server\MSSQL15.MSSQLSERVER\MSSQL\DATA\testDB.mdf',
      SIZE = 10MB,
      MAXSIZE = 100MB,
      FILEGROWTH = 10MB
  )
  LOG ON (
      NAME = testDB_log,
      FILENAME = 'C:\Program Files\Microsoft SQL Server\MSSQL15.MSSQLSERVER\MSSQL\DATA\testDB_log.ldf',
      SIZE = 5MB,
      MAXSIZE = 50MB,
      FILEGROWTH = 5MB
  );

MySQL Example with character set and collation:
CREATE DATABASE testDB
CHARACTER SET utf8mb4
COLLATE utf8mb4_general_ci;

Common Uses
- Create a separate database for a new application.
- Create a test database for development or quality assurance.
- Create a new tenant database in multi-tenant applications.

Exercise Question
What is the purpose of the SQL CREATE DATABASE statement?
- To create a new SQL database

Incorrect answers:
- To create a new table in an existing database (wrong)
- To delete an existing database (wrong)
- To modify an existing database (wrong)
